                <pb facs="0813" n="719" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg719"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Williams to Mr. Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-05-11"><hi rendition="#italic">May 11,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2968.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to acknowledge the receipt of the
                    Department’s telegram of the 9th instant. * * *</p>
                <p>In consequence I addressed a communication to the governor and captain-general in
                    the same sense almost word for word.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ramon O.
                    Williams.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
